+# Turn diff
+
+Codex tracks the net change of every file that `apply_patch` touches during a turn. It takes each file's baseline from the content the patch replaced, at the moment the patch applies, and sends the aggregate as `turn/diff/updated`. A client can receive that diff with the turn's prompt response. Clients opt in during initialization:
+
+```json
+{
+  "clientCapabilities": {
+    "_meta": {
+      "codex": {
+        "turnDiff": true
+      }
+    }
+  }
+}
+```
+
+When a turn completes, the `session/prompt` response carries the last diff Codex reported for that turn next to the existing `quota` key:
+
+```json
+{
+  "stopReason": "end_turn",
+  "_meta": {
+    "quota": { "...": "..." },
+    "codex": {
+      "turnDiff": {
+        "status": "reported",
+        "turnId": "019a...",
+        "root": "/Users/me/vault",
+        "diff": "diff --git a/notes/a.md b/notes/a.md\n--- a/notes/a.md\n+++ b/notes/a.md\n@@ -1 +1 @@\n-old\n+new\n"
+      }
+    }
+  }
+}
+```
+
+`diff` is Codex's unified Git diff, unchanged. It is an empty string when the turn changed no files. Its paths are relative to `root`: the nearest ancestor of the working directory that contains `.git`, or the working directory itself when there is none. The adapter resolves `root` before the turn starts, as Codex does.
+
+A diff larger than 8 MiB is not sent. The response then carries `{ "status": "unavailable", "turnId": "...", "reason": "tooLarge" }`.
+
+Only a completed turn carries the key. A cancelled prompt, a failed turn, and a local command that starts no turn do not.
+
+The diff has the same coverage as Codex's tracker. It omits changes made outside `apply_patch`, including shell commands, version-control commands, generators, and child processes.
+
+A client that does not opt in gets the same prompt response as before. AIR clients can keep using the [agent file-change report](air-extensions.md#agent-file-change-report), which sends the changed paths without the diff text.
